nodes.append({
 "id": 3, "lang": "Persian", "words": "dŭd «دود»; dŭdeh «دوده»; dŭdmân «دودمان»",
 "verdict": "confirmed",
 "derivation": "New Persian دود dūd continues Middle Persian dūd unchanged. دوده dūda is dūd plus the nominal suffix -a (< MP -ag; MacKenzie's dūdag), and carries both of the chart's senses: Borhān-e Qāṭeʿ p. 894 defines دوده as «دودمان و خانواده … و دود چراغ که بجهت ساختن مرکب و سیاهی گیرند», i.e. 'family' and 'lamp-black, soot' — the latter being literally the deposit of smoke, whence its use for making ink. Ferdowsī's line quoted in the box («کزاین دودهٔ سام شد رنگ و بوی») uses the 'lineage' sense, and Hübschmann, Pers. Studien no. 579, notes 'np. dūda \"Familie\" Firdausī I, 453 v. 334'. دودمان dūdmān is dūd + -mān 'dwelling' (MP mān 'house'), literally 'smoke-house' > 'family, dynasty'; Borhān p. 894: «دودمان … خاندان و خانواده و قبیله را گویند», with Moʿin's footnote «از: دود + مان (پسوند مان به‌معنی خانه)». (Wiktionary's Proto-Iranian *duHmáh for دود is the *dʰuh₂-mós formation and leaves the final -d unexplained; the *dūta- of Moʿin/Horn accounts for it better.)",
