   {"src": "CHEUNG", "where": "p. 400 s.v. *θuaxš (tuxš) 'to be busy, working on'", "stance": "contradicts", "note": "\"*MIDDLE PERSIAN: MMP twxs- 'to strive' … || (+ *ham-) BMP ʾndwh /andōh/ 'sorrow', MMP ʾndwxyn 'sad, sorrowful'\"; *SOGDIAN \"(+ *ham-) BSogd. ʾnt(ʾ)wxs … 'to strive'\"; *NWIR \"(+ *ham-) NP andōh 'anxious'\"."},
   {"src": "NYB", "where": "Manual of Pahlavi II, glossary p. 100", "stance": "partial", "note": "NYB_vol2_glossary.txt l. 1894: \"handōhakan [hndwhkn'] anxious … Arm. lw. andohakan 'disquieting, dreadful'\" — the page Moʿin cites; Nyberg gives the Middle Persian form but no Avestan antecedent."}
